  journalLore: The jutuls were here before the trees. They sleep for a hundred years at a time and wake up cross, with moss on their shoulders, and walk until they find whatever woke them.
  journalAdvice: 'Slow, and stone all over: blades skid off it. Stay out of its stamp and sweep and hit it as it recovers. Blunt weapons and fire do better than edges.'
